cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or essay, please cite it as below."
title: "In Tlilli, In Tlapalli: A Codicological Survey of the Codex Borgia and the Florentine Codex"
authors:
  - family-names: Stevenson
    given-names: Michael
type: dataset
abstract: >
  A physical-evidence dataset and comparative essay examining production
  methods, materials, and corrections in the Codex Borgia and the
  Florentine Codex, developed from an M.A. thesis (Art History, Arizona
  State University, 2003, chair: Emily Umberger).
keywords:
  - codicology
  - Codex Borgia
  - Florentine Codex
  - Mesoamerican manuscripts
  - watermarks
  - paleography
license: CC-BY-4.0
